Fixture note: backup-name ordering is load-bearing

expected_output.txt lines must match the recipe's listing order, and the
harness matcher checks lines in order. The listing order is bash glob
expansion order of "$BACKUP_DIR"/*.bak, which sorts by the current
locale's collation - C (CI) and en_US.UTF-8 (macOS) disagree whenever
punctuation would decide the order, e.g. a .just%2F name against a
.just_legacy name (the % sorts before _ in C, but the punctuation is
ignored in en_US.UTF-8 and the alphanumerics decide).

Every backup name in this fixture therefore shares the `.just%2F`
prefix and the names diverge first at an alphanumeric character
(aa < v2 < x < zz), so both collations produce the same order. Keep new
backup names on that pattern, and put differently-punctuated names
(legacy _-for-/ names) in a separate fixture - see
16_recipe_copilot_rollback_legacy_name, which exists for exactly that
reason.

Suggested in the Claude review of PR #434.